2,Traditional Cambodian musical instruments - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Traditional_Cambodian_musical_instruments,"March 23, 2026 - Traditional Cambodian musical instruments are the musical instruments used in the traditional and classical music of Cambodia. They comprise a wide range of wind, string, and percussion instruments, used by both the Khmer majority as well as the nation's ethnic minorities.",Khmer,Austro-Asiatic
3,Khmer Music | Asia Society,https://asiasociety.org/education/khmer-music,"July 25, 2017 - Khmer music consists of polyphonic stratification and is based predominantly on the pentatonic (five-tone) scale. It is built linearly, devoid of harmony in the Western sense. Musicians in a music ensemble have a collective melody in mind that ...",Khmer,Austro-Asiatic
4,"Austroasiatic languages | Mon-Khmer, Munda & Vietic | Britannica",https://www.britannica.com/topic/Austroasiatic-languages,"July 26, 1999 - The Austroasiatic languages are a family of approximately 150 languages spoken by over 65 million people scattered across Southeast Asia and eastern India. This language group is significant as a linguistic base for all Southeast Asian languages. Khmer, Mon, and Vietnamese are the most culturally significant Austroasiatic languages, with the longest recorded histories.",Khmer,Austro-Asiatic
5,The Music of Cambodia: A Rough Guide | Songlines,https://www.songlines.co.uk/the-rough-guide-to-world-music/the-music-of-cambodia-a-rough-guide,"During this period, a delicate classical dance style and accompanying court music were developed from the dances of maidens (apsaras) who performed at the temples to honour the gods, and the dance style the Khmer created went on to influence classical dance across the region.",Khmer,Austro-Asiatic
